1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[indistinct chatter and laughter]

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,000
[birds squawking]

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
[boy exhaling]

4
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
[theme music playing]

5
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
[Gon and Killua]
Ready? Go!

6
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
[both chomping]

7
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Kurapika!

8
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
-I'm happy for you.
-Huh?

9
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
The Spiders are dead.

10
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
And that means that you can finally focus
on your main goal, right?

11
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
You have to go out there and find them.
The eyes of your people.

12
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Gon...

13
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
And if there's anything we can do
to help you out, just--

14
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[snickering]

15
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
-[Gon] Why, you!
-[Killua yelping]

16
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
You did it first.
I was just getting revenge!

17
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
[Gon] I didn't do it on purpose!

18
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
-[Killua] You did so, you big liar.
-[chuckles]

19
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
[both grunting]

20
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
[chuckles]

21
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
What are you so upset about, huh?

22
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,000
We sold one piece and walked away
with a cool 355 million Jenny!

23
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
That's the problem.
It could have sold for a lot more.

24
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
[Leorio] We got plenty!

25
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Wrong. We could have gotten
well over 400 million for it,

26
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
if we'd just waited.

27
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Bad luck, that's what it is.

28
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
You sure take this seriously.

29
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Besides, even if we did get more,
it’s not like you would’ve seen any of it.

30
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
[Zepile] That's not the issue here.

31
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:43,000
If we take the money and run,
that’s 170 million apiece! [cackling]

32
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Are you really friends
with Gon and Killua?

33
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
-[phone ringing]
-I'm kidding, lighten up.

34
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Yeah, hello?

35
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Oh. Hey, Kurapika!

36
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Wow, it's been a while
since we were all together!

37
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Yeah.

38
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
[Gon] Where's Mr. Zepile?

39
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
[Leorio] Oh, he went back over
to pick up the check

40
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
and find some more loot to sell.

41
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Hey, you know something?

42
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
[Kurapika] What?

43
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
You've got this intensity about you.

44
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Your presence is a whole lot stronger
than it was.

45
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Really?

46
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Well, I wish I could say the same for you.

47
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
And you’ve also gotten
a lot more annoying!

48
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,000
[elevator dings]

49
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
[Leorio] Oh, yeah.
I heard you killed a Troupe member.

50
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:35,000
How the hell did you do that
when you only learned Nen recently?

51
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
If the reason you’re asking
is that you’re planning

52
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
to catch the Spiders yourself,
you can stop.

53
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
That's not the only reason.

54
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
You've mastered Nen and we want
to learn how too.

55
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Not just to catch the Spiders,
but because we'll need it in the future.

56
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
You don't want my advice.

57
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
I'm afraid it won't do you
any good, anyway.

58
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Because my power can only be used
against the Troupe.

59
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,000
[all gasp]

60
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
[Gon] A contract with conditions?

61
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Yes.

62
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Your mental state has
an incredibly powerful effect on your Nen.

63
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
The more determined you are,
the more powerful the Nen.

64
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
But the risk incurred is great, as well.

65
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
In exchange for stronger Nen,

66
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
I vowed that I would only use it
against the Spiders.

67
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
And I established a rule for myself.

68
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Oh, yeah? What kind of rule is it?

69
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:35,000
My chains must be used
exclusively on the Spiders.

70
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Or I will die as a result.

71
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
[both gasp]

72
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Hold on! What do you mean?

73
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
There is a Nen dagger in my heart.

74
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
If I break the rule, the blade
will pierce through, killing me.

75
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,000
The rule proves my resolve.
That's the contract with conditions.

76
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,000
My ability is the product of my pure
and unadulterated hatred.

77
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
It will only work when used
on the Spiders.

78
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:10,000
I'm telling you this because I trust you.
Don't tell anyone else.

79
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
What the hell?

80
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Why would you tell us something
that's so damn important?

81
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Huh?

82
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
I'm not really sure.

83
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Maybe I felt dispirited
because their leader is dead now.

84
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
It'll be fine if we keep it quiet.

85
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
No it won't.

86
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
One of the surviving members
has the power to read memories.

87
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:37,000
If the Spiders find out about this,
Kurapika's a dead man!

88
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
But she didn't learn anything last time.

89
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
You're right, but that's only
because we didn't know

90
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Kurapika was the chain user back then.

91
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Okay, so that means we just have
to stay away from them.

92
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Since they've already checked you out,
they think that you're clean.

93
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
[Killua]
There's also a guy called Nobunaga.

94
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
He's really dangerous.

95
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,000
He's looking for Kurapika
and he's still trying to get me and Gon.

96
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
[Leorio] But he doesn’t know
that you guys know Kurapika… does he?

97
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
-No.
-Well, then what's the problem?

98
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
Just keep your distance
from the memory reader.

99
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
You and everyone else
who knows Kurapika’s the chain user.

100
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
I've also been in contact with Hisoka.

101
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
[Leorio grunts]

102
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,000
With Hisoka?

103
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[Kurapika] He knows that I am
the chain user, as well.

104
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:28,000
We had made a pact, but his target,
the leader of the Phantom Troupe,

105
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
is dead gone now.

106
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
So I have no idea what he'll do.

107
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
[thunder rumbling]

108
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Hold on just a second.

109
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
What do you mean, we're leaving?

110
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,000
[Chrollo] Just like I told you.

111
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
We're leaving tonight.

112
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
We'll take the rest of the treasure.

113
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
And that's the end of it.

114
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
-[thunder rumbling]
-[Nobunaga] Not yet.

115
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
[Chrollo] What else is there?

116
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
[Nobunaga] We have to find the chain user.

117
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
-[Chrollo] You're obsessed.
-[Nobunaga] Damn right, I am.

118
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:09,000
We haven’t avenged Uvo’s death yet
and you want us to just pack and leave?

119
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
He’s gonna be bored in the next world

120
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
if we don’t send the chain user
to join him.

121
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Why don't you cut it out, Nobunaga?
The boss gave an order.

122
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:22,000
Right. The boss’ orders are absolute.

123
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:28,000
But I’ve got to wonder, are you really
speaking as our leader, Chrollo?

124
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Nobunaga, knock it off!

125
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Shut up! I'm trying to talk
to Chrollo, here.

126
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
[Chrollo] Before I can answer...

127
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Nobunaga...

128
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
I need you to answer my questions.

129
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,000
[thunder rumbling]

130
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
[Chrollo] Nobunaga,
I need you to answer my questions.

131
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
-What's your birthday?
-Huh?

132
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
[Chrollo] I asked what day you were born.

133
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
September 8th, in the year '70.

134
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
[Chrollo] Blood type?

135
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
[Nobunaga] B positive.

136
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,000
[Chrollo] Name?

137
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Nobunaga Hazama. You know that!

138
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
What is this?
What do you wanna know next, huh?

139
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Nothing. That's enough.

140
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Write it all down. Here.

141
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Write it down?
You could’ve said that to begin with.

142
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Huh? The hell is this?

143
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Your fortune in verse.
One hundred percent accurate.

144
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:57,000
I can tell the future, a skill I stole
from Nostrade's daughter.

145
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
And you're sure
that it's completely accurate?

146
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
[Chrollo] Each of the four verses predicts
what's going to happen in that week.

147
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:12,000
"Forever set, a previous moon is lost.
The others mourn him with ceremony grand.

148
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,000
The wolf alone misses out
on morning frost,

149
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
and seeks frost moon’s shadow
across the land.

150
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
Harvest barren, wine spilled,

151
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,000
lovers slumber
beside the bloody Scarlet Eyes.

152
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:29,000
Though cut in half shall be your number,
unhindered the spider flies."

153
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:36,000
This is the fortune
Nostrade's daughter gave me yesterday.

154
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:42,000
It says a precious moon has been lost,
so is that...

155
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
It's Uvo.

156
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,000
[gasps lightly]

157
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
[Chrollo]
That girl didn't know anything about Uvo.

158
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
In fact, she'd never heard of any of us.

159
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Yet she was able to predict our attack
on the Mafia auction.

160
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:02,000
And there were fans
of her fortune-telling among the Ten Dons.

161
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:06,000
I get it. That’s why the first time
we attacked,

162
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
somebody had already moved
the merchandise to a new location.

163
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Kinda curious.
What was Nobunaga's fortune?

164
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:18,000
My hand wrote it itself.
I have no idea what it is.

165
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Nobunaga can tell you.

166
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
[Shalnark] Well, what's it say?

167
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Come next week,
five of us will most likely die.

168
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Oh, yeah? Does it say which five?

169
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[Nobunaga]
No. I can't figure any of this out.

170
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Well, I kind of understand
the second poem.

171
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
The spider losing half its number.

172
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
The spider would be us, wouldn't it?

173
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
[Nobunaga] Yeah.

174
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
And the limbs would be the members,
so half would be six.

175
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
That means five more after Uvo.

176
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:56,000
The very same line appeared
in my fortune too.

177
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
[Shizuku] Let me see that.

178
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Hey, Boss. Do you think
you can tell my fortune?

179
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:13,000
"Forever set, a precious moon is lost.
The others mourn him with ceremony grand.

180
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
But lonely not, be the moon of frost.

181
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Soon your blood will join
his grave of sand.

182
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:25,000
In the chamber of treasure ill-gotten,
there is no choice but endless sleep.

183
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Your greatest fear should solitude be,
lest upon your lonesome form he creep.

184
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Just as I expected.
Looks like I'm gonna die next week.

185
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Seriously?

186
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Yeah, you see?
I only got two poems in mine.

187
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:45,000
And look, Pakunoda and Shalnark
are gonna die too.

188
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,000
-Oh?
-Really?

189
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
How do you know it's Pakunoda
and Shalnark?

190
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:55,000
It think the months mentioned here
refer to Phantom Troupe members.

191
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:00,000
The frost moon is November.
Uvo's the 11th member, the 11th month.

192
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
[Chrollo] Exactly.

193
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:06,000
The harvest moon is in September,
the wine moon is August,

194
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
and the lover’s moon is June.

195
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:13,000
This refers to numbers six,
eight and nine.

196
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:18,000
And "barren" is mentioned,
which I believe implies death.

197
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:21,000
I’m just not certain
who “Scarlet Eyes” refers to.

198
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Well, it isn't one of us.

199
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:26,000
I'm guessing it might be a reference
to the chain user.

200
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,000
[gasps]

201
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:30,000
[Pakunoda] Scarlet Eyes.
I remember now.

202
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
The clan whose eyes turned red.

203
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
[Feitan] Then there was a survivor?

204
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
[Shalnark] So it would seem.

205
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Will he die too?

206
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,000
It's hard to tell.

207
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,000
It doesn’t say anything other
than the guy is bloody.

208
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
[Shalnark] Nobunaga, this means
if we fight the chain user,

209
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:52,000
we'll suffer serious casualties
and lose half our members.

210
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Your ability can be replaced
as easily as mine,

211
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
but not Shizuku's or Pakunoda's.

212
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
The Troupe can't afford
to lose either of them.

213
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,000
[thunder crashing]

214
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Today is Saturday of the first week.

215
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
So if we leave now and return home,

216
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:15,000
then that means we can avoid
running into the chain user next week.

217
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
The best thing about these fortunes
is that if we pay attention...

218
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,000
they tell us how to avoid catastrophe.

219
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,000
If we leave here
without fighting the chain user,

220
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:32,000
this fortune is 100 percent certain
not to come to pass.

221
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Nobunaga, you and Uvo
were our attack unit.

222
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
You were already prepared to die.

223
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:46,000
I believe that both of you accepted
that role of your own free will.

224
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
[Nobunaga] Yeah, that's right.

225
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
[Chrollo] Shizuku, Paku and Shal
collect intelligence.

226
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
They provide our support.

227
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
You could even call them our lifelines.

228
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:04,000
And your duty is to serve as their shield.
You agree with that assessment?

229
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Yeah. Yeah, I do.

230
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,000
[Hisoka] Wait.

231
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
You should tell the other members'
fortunes now.

232
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
It’s quite possible
that they could provide additional clues

233
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
for how to avoid the prophecy.

234
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,000
[Killua] What do we do?

235
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,000
Now that we all know
about Kurapika’s secret,

236
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,000
it’s dangerous to wait.

237
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,000
If Gon or I get captured again,
we won’t be able to escape.

238
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
But we do have Kurapika with us now.

239
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:39,000
So we need to take them out
before they can recover or run.

240
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
And we know where their current base is.

241
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,000
If we take too long,
it'll give them a chance to get away.

242
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
That means we need to move fast.

243
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
They could be making a getaway plan
as we speak.

244
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
We don't have time to overthink it.

245
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,000
That woman, the one who reads memories,
is a threat.

246
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:10,000
But now that their leader’s dead,
I’ll do what Gon suggests

247
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,000
and focus on recovering
my brethren's eyes.

248
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
-Seriously?
-Yeah.

249
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,000
And you're sure about this?

250
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Look, it's obvious he's made up his mind.

251
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,000
You can try all you want,
there’s no changing it now.

252
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
I'm sorry.

253
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
But thanks.
I do appreciate the information.

254
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
[phone ringing]

255
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
It's from Hisoka.

256
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,000
[gasps]

257
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
[Hisoka] The corpses were fake.

258
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,000
[Gon] Kurapika?

259
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,000
The corpses were fake.

260
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,000
[Leorio gasps]
You mean the Troupe members?

261
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Yeah. The ones we thought
were dead, aren't!

262
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Of course! A Conjurer could have pulled
that off easily!

263
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Damn it! Why didn't I realize this sooner?

264
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,000
The situation has changed.
Now what?

265
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,000
We're here to help.

266
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Right.

267
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Yeah.

268
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,000
[phone ringing]

269
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Hello?

270
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
[Melody] Kurapika, it's me.

271
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Oh. Melody. What is it?

272
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
[Melody] The community has called off
the hunt for the remaining Troupe members.

273
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,000
What?

274
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
[Melody] We just received word
that they come from Meteor City.

275
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,000
[Kurapika] The Troupe? Really?

276
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:38,000
And apparently the order came directly
from the Ten Dons themselves.

277
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,000
They even took the offer for reward money
off the table.

278
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:45,000
[thunder rumbling]

279
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
[Killua] The reward's been rescinded?

280
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Seriously?

281
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
So the Phantom Troupe
comes from Meteor City.

282
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
It makes sense.
Their identities are still unknown

283
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:02,000
And the cops haven’t caught them yet.
That would explain all of that.

284
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,000
What is Meteor City?

285
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,000
A place populated by people
who don’t exist,

286
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,000
for all intents and purposes.

287
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,000
There’s a whole city like that?

288
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Yeah. Officially, the town
has a population of zero.

289
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:19,000
But it’s said that there are at least
ten million people who live there.

290
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:25,000
It started off as a dump
over 1,500 years ago.

291
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:29,000
You were allowed to dump anything there.

292
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:34,000
And whatever trash was thrown away,
that’s what people lived off of.

293
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,000
-Trash, weapons, even people.
-[baby crying]

294
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
[Leorio] No matter what’s left there,

295
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
the residents take it in
without a second thought.

296
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:49,000
I’ve heard people from Meteor City
share a bond thinner than water,

297
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
but at the same time thicker than blood.

298
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Also, there’s an organization

299
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:01,000
that provides gold and weapons
under the pretext of dumping garbage.

300
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Namely, the Mafia community.

301
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:08,000
What? What do you mean?
The Mafia is hunting the Troupe!

302
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:12,000
In return, the Mafia picks new recruits
from among the residents.

303
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:16,000
These are people
who basically don't exist, remember?

304
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Perfect for criminal activity.

305
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
The Troupe managed to destroy
the intimate business relationship

306
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,000
that used to exist between the Mafia
and Meteor City.

307
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Even after all that's happened,

308
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,000
the Mafia wants to retain the relationship
with Meteor City.

309
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:48,000
[Hisoka] "With eyes of red,
a customer comes to call.

310
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Half of him an angel, the other death.

311
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Secrets of the moons tell him all.

312
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:58,000
Those of the frost moon,
he awaits with bated breath.

313
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
On the day of the sun,
under this customer’s care,

314
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,000
alone with the man of cross reversed...

315
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Removed from the calendar
is the false hare.

316
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,000
With six months gone, the year is cursed."

317
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:22,000
What does your fortune say?
Show me.

318
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:31,000
I don't recommend it.
It might startle you.

319
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
Oh, just let me see it.

320
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Very well.

321
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
[gasps]

322
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
[Pakunoda] Everyone, look at this.

323
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,000
A customer who has eyes of red?

324
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Wait, the secrets of the moons?

325
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Hold on a minute, those would be
our secrets, wouldn’t they?

326
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,000
[Franklin] Hisoka, what is this?

327
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Let me see!

328
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,000
[gasps lightly]

329
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,000
[Nobunaga]
"A red-eyed customer comes into view.

330
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Of bartering and sweet deals he croons.

331
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:09,000
The sword of law he plunges into you,
and makes off with secrets of the moons.

332
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:13,000
The 11-legged spider longs for home.

333
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Five more legs shall break
before it's done.

334
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:21,000
But from your shelter do not roam,
for of those five, you shall be one."

335
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Hisoka.

336
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:29,000
Did you sell out Uvo?

337
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,000
Answer me!

338
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
[narrator]
The words in Hisoka’s fortune changed

339
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,000
the moment it was passed to Pakunoda.

340
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:49,000
The question is... what could that mean?

341
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:53,000
[theme music playing]

342
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:01,000
-[Gon] Coming up, Gon...
-[Killua] And Killua's...

343
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

344
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,000
-I'm Gon!
-I'm Killua!

345
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

346
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Today, we'll introduce Bonolenov!
He's a Troupe member.

347
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:12,000
His face, body and powers
are completely covered by bandages.

348
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:16,000
[both] Spin, spin, spin, spin!

349
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Allies and Lies."

350
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
-[Killua] My Highness.
-[Gon] Your Highness?

351
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:30,000
-[Killua] His Highness, Killua!
-[Gon] Yeah, yeah.
